WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.435 --> 00:00:02.935
(funky music)

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:09.105
(camera clicks)

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.433
- Okay, fine.

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:13.030
I know this guys been watching me.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.000
This is the 14 hundred dollar
Samsung Galaxy S20 Ultra

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.710
with one of the craziest zoom lenses

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.233
on a smartphone to date.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.050
This is Michael McKeever,

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.913
a New York City private investigator.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.620
- I've been a private
eye for over 30 years.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.960
Well I work in the street a
lot, I do a lot of surveillance

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.710
so being out of my car
and getting pictures

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.820
of people without them knowing,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.370
that's just another day at
the office for me, really.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.120
- [Narrator] Sure,
having a better zoom lens

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.730
has some appeal in every day life.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.283
Yeah, for birding and things.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.180
But I couldn't think of a real reason

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.620
anyone needed an 100x
zoom on their smartphone

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.980
except of course if your job is

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.520
to watch people without them knowing.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.860
So we had Mike test in three situations

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.440
to see how the Galaxy S20 Ultra compares

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.750
to the iPhone 11 Pro Max,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.770
his go to Sony camcorder,

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:04.413
and the one thousand
dollar Nikon CoolPix P1000.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.190
Test one: from a car
into an apartment window.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.880
Distance: about 50 feet.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.230
Okay, maybe I set the scene inside of it.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.590
- The Samsung takes an awesome picture.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.810
We wouldn't normally be shooting

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.730
into someone's apartment like this.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.370
But it is an impressive camera.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.100
- [Narrator] Turns out, PIs don't really

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.400
shoot into people's homes

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.930
because it can break privacy laws.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.330
When comparing shots, it
was nuts how much better

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.523
the Samsung was compared to the iPhone.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.810
That's because the Galaxy S20
has this new telephoto lens.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.060
But what Samsung calls
a folded zoom mechanism.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.290
It uses the phone's three lenses to create

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.450
10X hybrid optical zoom,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.070
then magnifies that for 100x digital zoom.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.910
That's a lot of marketing jargon.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:58.920
But what you need to know

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.490
is that shots between
10x and 30x are crisp.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:05.410
Shots up to 100x, not so much.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.120
- But the quality of the pictures is good,

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.210
until you get to the really max zoom.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.043
- [Narrator] As you may have guessed,

00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:15.980
that Nikon's 125x optical zoom
produced a crazy clear image.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.790
Just look at the detail in my earring.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.360
The Sony, with its 30x optical zoom,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.923
wasn't too shabby either.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.480
Test two: a moving subject.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.923
Distance: about 150 feet.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.420
- When you go to the hundreds,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.750
it's hard to even find her in the frame.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.583
- [Narrator] The results.

00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:41.810
It's so hard to take a
shot of a moving object

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.433
past the 30x setting.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.080
- The tripod I would never do.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.430
Unless I was a wedding photographer maybe.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.920
- [Narrator] And even then,
the shots at 30x were clearer

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.720
and said a lot more about the scene.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.850
Nothing beat the Nikon though for getting

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.150
the action of the pic.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.680
For moving shots like this,

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.570
Mike prefers his camcorder.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.463
And I see why.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.523
By the way, it was a scratch, not a pick.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.650
Test three: text on a computer screen.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.960
Distance: about 15 feet.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.680
I wrote the first line in 14 point font.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.373
The second in 24 point.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.640
The results.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.620
The Galaxy S20 Ultra can
really capture some things

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.920
you may not want people
seeing on your screen.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.310
- It's good, the quality
of the picture is good.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.070
As far as the magnification,
the 30x is really good.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.660
Would really be useful.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:33.660
- [Narrator] And while the quality isn't

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.950
as good as the Nikon

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.983
or even Mike's trusty camcorder,

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.640
it's a heck of a lot more discrete.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.833
- How you been Mike?

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:47.210
- Good.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.043
- Been watching me?

00:03:48.043 --> 00:03:49.082
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:49.082 --> 00:03:50.730
So would you buy one?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.563
- Would I buy one?

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.660
I would buy one, yeah, I mean I'm kind of

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.700
locked in on apple now
with so many things,

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.050
but yeah it's definitely
an improvement I think

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.550
as far as cameras go.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.870
- [Narrator] I agree and the
shots are really impressive

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.130
for a smartphone.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.780
But do we want everyone to
have PI tools in their pocket?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.420
- Some guys focus on trying
to get the best equipment.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.530
I don't really ascribe to that.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.960
I feel like, Eric Clapton's
not a great guitar player

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.330
because he bought the most
expensive guitar in the world.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.530
It has to do with the
skill of the operator.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.500
- [Narrator] Still, I'd close the windows.

